WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:05.105
Any joy here is fleeting.

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:07.507
This dance could be their last.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.709
Russian soldiers, most convicts here

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.511
living it up hours before

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:13.680
being sent to the front lines.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.715
They fight to be pardoned.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.617
But here, over half died.

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.652
At the front, survivors said

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.021
even some after

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.356
they've lived through the battles

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.624
of Viktor.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.693
Seven was jailed for armed robbery

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:27.594
and assault,

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:29.062
but taken out of prison

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.463
and thrown into the worst

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:33.266
fighting outside of Soledar

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:35.869
His unit joking here

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:37.470
before they assault a factory

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.972
the next day suffered

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.640
catastrophic casualties.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.275
He told his wife

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:43.710
Victor survived

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.578
but as he lay injured in hospital,

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:48.048
he feared being dragged from his bed

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:50.283
and executed for poor performance.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:53.286
This is his last message to his wife.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:23.983
days later.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:24.617
His wife

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.719
got a closed coffin back

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:28.555
after a call from a soldier

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:29.889
who said Victor had died

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.724
from shrapnel injuries.

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:34.127
He's buried here outside Moscow

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:37.430
There's something

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.331
very different, though,

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:39.265
about civilian life

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.500
to many of the prisoners

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.801
sent to the front line

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:42.902
to make up for Russia's

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.238
devastating casualties.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.440
Most are sent by a shadowy private

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.342
military contractor, Wagner,

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:50.443
who in this propaganda

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.077
video

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:52.312
are keen to portray

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.247
rare survivors coming back.

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.049
Joyful, grateful, even,

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:56.883
and last week

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.151
claimed to have stopped

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:00.386
recruiting in prisons altogether.

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:02.822
But seven and several convicts CNN

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.090
has spoken to said

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:04.958
they were hired

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.626
from jail directly

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.095
by the Russian Ministry of Defense.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.964
It's a remarkable use of convicts

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.632
directly by Moscow.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.400
And Ukrainian intelligence says it's

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.236
captured them on the front line.

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:19.506
even among

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:21.541
Russian prisoners of war in Ukraine,

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:22.976
there are now those recruited

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:23.710
into the private

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.478
companies of the defense ministry

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:27.480
of the Russian Federation.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.481
They emphasize to us

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.416
that they are not forgotten,

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:31.818
but officially invited

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.620
by the defense ministry

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.692
Here we hear echoes of internal squabbles

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.961
in the Russian military leadership role.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.330
Wagner's presence is being diluted

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.198
with convicts

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:46.633
directly controlled

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:48.601
by the defense chief's Shoigu

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.236
and Gerasimov.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.871
So we hear someone

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.406
recruitment has surged.

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:54.340
These government figures

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.776
showing a sudden 27,000 drop

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:58.711
in the prison population last year

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.513
when the scheme was just underway

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:02.715
with no apparent amnesty to explain it.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:06.486
There is a large proportion have died

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:07.086
with this

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:08.388
 Wagner training video

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:10.356
showing one of the reckless tactics

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:11.257
prisoners are used

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.593
for charging forwards together

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:14.727
at the enemy

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:15.428
surveillance

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:18.631
that was part of a unit called 08807.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:20.800
And its other frontline survivors

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.969
know how hard it is to stay alive

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.671
under the Ministry of Defense.

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:27.941
We spoke to several

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:29.475
from their hospital beds

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.244
hiding their identity.

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:33.046
A former soldier jailed on drugs

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:35.648
charges described being sent back twice

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:36.883
to the front while injured.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:55.802
Another convicted on manslaughter says

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:58.304
half his unit became casualties.

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.586
It's a recruitment scheme, ensnaring

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:14.754
whoever it can.

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:17.790
Some aren't even Russian

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:20.026
In this ghoulish ceremony,

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.027
Wagner honors

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:23.296
Tanzanian student Nemes Tarimo.

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:25.965
He was detained on drugs charges

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:27.834
while on a study exchange

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.168
here at a Red Square

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.738
Christmas event in a justice system

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.640
that's notoriously corrupt.

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:36.476
His family in Tanzania said

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:38.478
they did not even know he'd been arrested

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:39.312
when they learned

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:41.281
he'd been killed in the war.

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:44.851
since his childhood

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:46.886
Nemes was a very obedient boy.

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:48.221
He wasn't a scamp.

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:50.256
He was a very religious person.

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:51.190
When he was alive,

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.225
we never heard about it.

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:53.226
But now that he's dead,

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:54.494
we're told he was arrested

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:56.362
for drug related offenses.

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.264
It really hurts us as a family.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.768
he never even had a dream

00:05:01.768 --> 00:05:03.970
of becoming a soldier.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:05.905
His body was returned,

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:09.008
closed entombing yet another story of

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:11.144
how life is thrown away at the front.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:14.647
Nick Paton Walsh, CNN, London.

